  "notes": "A photographed checkerboard: one cell squares of Ink and Paper with 10% of cells flipped by noise. A PERFECT one cell checkerboard is a fixed point of the 3x3 majority rule (each cell sees itself and its four diagonals, five of nine, measured 2026-10-30: 95.8% isolated after any number of passes), so it could never satisfy H-pipe-2; the noisy one is what the rule smooths (measured on the family: about 15 to 25% isolated after one pass, 4 to 7% after two), which is what CA_ONE_PASS must fail. Mean L about 125 and nothing saturated: Attic. What survives is scattered small blobs; platform and landmark counts are not designed, so null; a climb by blobs or tabs.",
